<title>FRANCE: U.S. top source of Paris Jan-Feb air cargo imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top source of Paris Jan-Feb air cargo imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the main source  for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-February 1997, airport authority(ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The main countries of origin for ADP imports in January-February 1997, with percentage change on the same months last year in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>1.   United States				22,706    down   1.3 pct</p>
<p>2.   Japan					   3,982	up  53.5</p>
<p>3.   India					   3,753    down  14.6</p>
<p>4.   Canada					  3,677    down  19.6</p>
<p>5.   UK						3,173	up  17.0</p>
<p>6.   Hong Kong				     2,713    down   4.8</p>
<p>7.   Germany					 2,540	up  30.0</p>
<p>8.   Thailand					2,181	up  44.6</p>
<p>9.   Senegal					 2,087	up  23.6</p>
<p>10.  Italy					   1,704    down   6.6</p>
<p>11.  Kenya					   1,383    down  27.1</p>
<p>12.  Singapore				     1,352	up  64.2</p>
<p>13.  Morocco					 1,273    down  32.3</p>
<p>14.  French West Indies			  1,135	up  14.7</p>
<p>15.  Argentina				     1,097	up   5.7</p>
<p>16.  Korea					   1,081	up  48.5</p>
<p>17.  China					   1,023	up  66.8</p>
<p>18.  Switzerland				     998	up  28.4</p>
<p>19.  Egypt					     978	up  41.8</p>
<p>20.  Brazil					    972	up  20.6</p>
<p>Total: 59,808  tonnes Overall January-February 1997  import traffic to CDG and Orly totalled 83,417 tonnes, an increase of 3.8 percent on the same period last year, ADP, figures show. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
